{
  "note": [
    "Engine cases for the DATED-REGIME exhibit (gst-rate.l4, spec §15).",
    "",
    "WHAT THESE COVER, and it is the whole point of the exhibit: the SAME model",
    "answers differently for different RULE DATES, in two real engines, driven",
    "entirely by half-open date intervals on a UNIQUE decision table.",
    "",
    "`GST rate percent` lowers to four rules and therefore THREE seams --",
    "2024-01-01, 2023-01-01 and 1994-04-01 -- and every one of them is straddled",
    "by a day-of / day-before pair: D+E, G+H, I+J. That is what pins the",
    "closed-low / open-high convention, and it is per-seam on purpose: an earlier",
    "version straddled only 2024-01-01, so an off-by-one on the middle interval's",
    "low end, or on the floor row's `< date(\"1994-04-01\")`, would have passed",
    "every case. Delete any of the three pairs and that hole comes back.",
    "",
    "`{\"$date\": \"YYYY-MM-DD\"}` is the fixture vocabulary's only way to say",
    "\"this is a FEEL date\", and it is deliberately an explicit tag rather than",
    "an ISO-shape sniff: both harnesses convert by declared type, never by",
    "appearance (see KieDmnCheck.jsonToFeel's BigDecimal note).",
    "",
    "WHAT THEY DO NOT COVER, so a green run is not read as more than it is:",
    "  * `the rules in force include` is a businessKnowledgeModel as of Phase 5",
    "    (tier 2), so it is no longer a decision the harness can assert, and",
    "    `change` is no longer an inputData -- it is the BKM's formalParameter,",
    "    bound per invocation. Nothing in THIS artifact invokes it (the dated",
    "    chains inlined its guards into interval endpoints, which is D2's whole",
    "    point), so its logic is exercised here only through those intervals.",
    "  * the floor row's answer is the ASSUME bottom, which L4 refuses to",
    "    evaluate. Here it is an ordinary DMN input, and -1 is a sentinel chosen",
    "    because no real rate could be negative, so a floor-row hit is",
    "    unmistakable in the harness output."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "A. the 2024 regime",
      "context": {
        "RULES_EFFECTIVE_DATE": {
          "$date": "2024-06-30"
        },
        "supply_value": 1000,
        "no_GST_rate_exists_before_commencement_on_1994_04_01": -1
      },
      "expect": {
        "the_2024_rate_change": {
          "$date": "2024-01-01"
        },
        "the_2023_rate_change": {
          "$date": "2023-01-01"
        },
        "GST_commenced": {
          "$date": "1994-04-01"
        },
        "GST_rate_percent": 9,
        "tourist_refund_minimum_spend": 100,
        "GST_payable_on": 90
      }
